--- commit message head
KS-999: getUserById awaits fromRow, so a failure inside fromRow reaches the KS-253 classifier (503, not a raw 500)

AUTH SERVICE, not auth logic. getUserById returned fromRow(...) unawaited
from inside its try. fromRow is async and reads the subject DEK, itself a DB
read, so a rejection inside it was never caught: on an encrypted row, the
normal production path, pool starvation there surfaced as a raw error (500)
instead of ServiceUnavailable (503). The one-word fix is
return await fromRow(...). A non-infrastructure failure, a decrypt failure
included, is still rethrown as-is, and is now logged by the catch.

- New ks999-getuserbyid-awaits-fromrow.test.ts (renamed from the READY's
  auto-name): an sdek: row so fromRow takes its getDek read; a getDek
  infrastructure rejection becomes "temporarily unavailable", and the
  classifier logs it; controls for a non-infrastructure rejection, the
  query()-side path (KS-963) and an untouched row.
- ks949-platform-admin-seed-identity.test.ts, ticket items 3 and 4:
  - the logger mock captures error like info/warn;
  - the KS-963 infrastructure cell also asserts the operator log;
  - the cell titled "it is the UNAWAITED fromRow that lets it escape" is
    renamed to what its assertion proves (a non-prod control);
  - the KS-963 header notes KS-999.
- userRepo.ts's KS-963 doc comment no longer says the await is
  "deliberately NOT done here"; it states what KS-999 changed.

Part of KS-999. Item 2 (the four calling route families) is the QA gate's.
The five sibling unawaited returns (:442, :508, :581, :590, :623) are
KS-1186, not this PR. KS-1168's :1017/:1061 are untouched.

Product line and ks999 cells authored by the local model (Ornith) from a
Wednesday-written brief; source-read by Wednesday; applied and re-run by the
seat A successor, who made the test-file and comment edits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

